WEBVTT

00:00.320 --> 00:06.320
Hello, my name is Fabio Brescia and today I'll talk to you about electric machines.

00:13.680 --> 00:20.560
In the last period we see the trend of the most of all automotive brands to switch their focus

00:20.560 --> 00:27.680
to the electric motors. We see this trend for fight the CO2 emission and try to reduce it.

00:27.680 --> 00:36.560
For motor drives we mean that devices that convert the onboard electrical energy to desired mechanical

00:36.560 --> 00:44.560
motion and they are the main technology for the hybrid and electric vehicle. Meanwhile electric

00:44.560 --> 00:53.680
machines are the key element of motor drive technology. The general requirements of electric

00:53.680 --> 01:02.160
machines for automotive are high torque density and high power density, wide speed range covering

01:02.160 --> 01:10.000
low speed creeping and high speed cruising to cover all the speed of the car without a gearbox,

01:10.720 --> 01:20.320
high efficiency over wide torque and speed ranges to reduce the losses power, wide constant power

01:20.320 --> 01:27.040
operating capability, low acoustic noise to the comfort of the driver, reasonable cost.

01:29.200 --> 01:36.240
Electric device can be defined as an electromechanical device for converting electrical energy into

01:36.240 --> 01:44.800
mechanical energy. In the right you can see the scheme of the typical architecture to convert electrical

01:44.800 --> 01:52.960
energy from the electric source into mechanical energy on the mechanical load. So this is the basic

01:53.600 --> 02:02.160
architecture of motion control system. We can see electric source that provides the energy to the drive

02:02.160 --> 02:13.120
system in the automotive field is the battery package. Power electronic converter that interfaces the motor with the power source and provides the motor with adjustable voltage

02:13.120 --> 02:33.120
current current and or frequency. The controller provides the appropriate control signals to the power converter by comparing the input command for speed and position with the actual values measured through sensors.

02:33.120 --> 02:40.800
The electric motor is the electric motor. The electric motor is the electric motor is the main device that converts the electric energy to the mechanical energy.

02:41.600 --> 02:51.760
The sensor needs to return the position or the velocity or the current of the actuator to the motion controller in order to close the control loops.

02:52.880 --> 03:01.440
The mechanical components transform the motion of the actuator into the desired load motion.

03:03.520 --> 03:14.560
In this lesson we can see in particular the electric motors. Just a reminder an electric motor converts the electrical energy into mechanical energy.

03:15.120 --> 03:26.640
The main layout of the electric motor consists in a cylindrical structure with a fixed part called stator and a moving one called rotor.

03:26.640 --> 03:36.960
We can find windings or permanent magnets in both of the structures to achieving different electrical and magnetic performances.

03:37.840 --> 03:46.000
The energy conversion happens in the interaction between the magnetic field of the two structures.

03:46.000 --> 03:57.200
We can see the main quantities of the electric machines.

03:57.200 --> 04:06.400
We can see the main quantities of the electric machines.

04:06.400 --> 04:16.240
In a motor, the induced EMF always acts to reduce the current in the loop.

04:16.800 --> 04:20.400
That's why it's called the back EMF.

04:20.400 --> 04:32.400
Faraday-Numann-Lens law establishes that the induced current in a loop is in the direction that creates a magnetic field that opposes

04:32.960 --> 04:38.000
the change in magnetic flux through the area enclosed by the loop.

04:38.720 --> 04:44.800
The induced current tends to keep the original magnetic flux through the circuit from changing.

04:44.800 --> 04:50.480
Here you can find the definition of the torque.

05:02.720 --> 05:08.320
In this slide we can see a first classification of the all-electric machines.

05:08.320 --> 05:16.560
In this lesson we will focus on the motors with permanent magnets and the induction motors.

05:17.120 --> 05:25.040
But first we must talk to the DC motors to understand how the technologies start their history.

05:31.200 --> 05:37.760
The benefits of the DC machines are that they can be used for simple operation

05:37.760 --> 05:42.560
with a simple motor control because the speed is proportional to the voltage.

05:43.520 --> 05:46.160
They are cheapest and simplest motor.

05:47.360 --> 05:51.600
The disadvantages are that requires high maintenance,

05:52.160 --> 05:55.760
daily generate sparks and they have a short life.

05:56.320 --> 06:00.000
All these problems are due to the presence of the brush.

06:02.000 --> 06:05.360
Motor technology is very mature and well developed,

06:05.920 --> 06:11.520
but for the automatic brand is no longer attractive for electric vehicle propulsion.

06:12.800 --> 06:19.840
It is no longer attractive for all the disadvantages of the DC motor and the demand of

06:20.720 --> 06:25.680
high efficiency, high power density and maintenance-free operation.

06:25.680 --> 06:31.680
On the right you can find the basic architecture of the DC machine.

06:32.800 --> 06:40.240
You can see the stator, external, equipped with salient poles, works as an inductor

06:40.240 --> 06:46.720
and can be realized with excitation windings or with permanent magnets.

06:46.720 --> 06:54.640
The final rotor, consisting of a cylinder of magnetic material, works as an armature.

06:55.280 --> 07:04.160
On the periphery of the rotor are uniformly distributed slots where the active conductors are hosed.

07:04.960 --> 07:09.760
The set of active conductors constitutes a closed circuit.

07:09.760 --> 07:15.120
The part in the air between the stator and rotor is called air gap.

07:15.120 --> 07:19.600
In this area, the magnetic field has the greatest intensity.

07:20.320 --> 07:25.200
The rotator is mounted on the same shaft as the rotor.

07:25.200 --> 07:32.960
This is for the purpose of supplied windings with the power supply voltage and ensure that the torque generated

07:32.960 --> 07:39.440
by the current that passes through is constant or at least any direction.

07:39.440 --> 07:50.080
The brush scrolls on the collector and electrically connect it to the external terminals of the machine.

07:50.640 --> 08:00.000
The presence of the system commutator brushes causes various issues, mainly the continuous maintenance

08:00.000 --> 08:03.760
required and undesired sparking.

08:03.760 --> 08:22.400
In this slide, you can find the working principle of the DC machines.

08:26.400 --> 08:32.480
The DC machine can work as a motor if the direction of the voltages and the currents

08:32.480 --> 08:34.240
are those shown in the picture.

08:36.720 --> 08:43.520
The E is made greater than V, the armature current is reversed and the machine switches

08:44.160 --> 08:53.360
to operate as a brake because the torque reverses becoming negative and instead of being a driving force

08:53.360 --> 08:55.360
it becomes braking.

08:55.360 --> 09:04.720
The DC machine in this condition works as a generator so it takes the energy from the load

09:04.720 --> 09:11.680
and converts it into electricity that can be dissipated or recovered.

09:12.960 --> 09:19.120
In this slide, you can see the four quadrant of operation of the DC machines.

09:19.120 --> 09:27.120
In this part, we will talk about the inverter.

09:27.120 --> 09:34.000
This device transforms the DC quantities in quantities in AC.

09:35.360 --> 09:40.960
The inverter design depends on the technology of power devices.

09:40.960 --> 09:51.920
Nowadays, the insulated gate bipolar transistor-based inverter is most attractive and has been widely

09:51.920 --> 09:54.560
accepted by modern electric vehicles.

09:55.680 --> 10:03.440
The selection of power devices is based on the voltage rating is at least twice the nominal battery voltage.

10:03.440 --> 10:11.280
The current rating is large enough so that there is no need to connect several power devices in parallel.

10:11.840 --> 10:19.600
The switching speed is sufficiently high to suppress motor harmonics and acoustic noise.

10:20.720 --> 10:29.200
Classified inverters of induction or permanent magnet motor into voltage-fed and current-fed types.

10:29.200 --> 10:37.440
But the current-fed inverters are rarely used for electric vehicle propulsion because of the need

10:38.400 --> 10:42.720
of a large series inductance to emulate a current source.

10:44.320 --> 10:51.120
In electric vehicle propulsion, it is preferred to use voltage-fed inverters because they are very simple

10:51.120 --> 10:53.600
and can have power flow in either direction.

10:53.600 --> 10:59.680
The control strategies can be classified as PWM or six-steps.

11:01.040 --> 11:09.760
The structure of the inverter is the same but changes the switching control technique of the various static switches.

11:11.520 --> 11:21.040
For PWM, it is the acronym of pulse-width modulation, so the period is the same but width changes.

11:21.040 --> 11:25.280
The PWM control is the comparison between

11:26.560 --> 11:39.120
modulating sinusoid of amplitude as and frequency fs and triangular carrier wave of constant amplitude at and frequency ft

11:39.680 --> 11:46.000
with at greater than as and ft greater than fs.

11:46.000 --> 11:54.320
When the value assumed by one of the modulators exceeds that of the triangular carrier,

11:54.320 --> 11:58.960
the switch s of the corresponding phase is turned on.

12:00.000 --> 12:07.600
When the value assumed by one of the modulators is less than that of the triangular carrier,

12:07.600 --> 12:08.800
it is turned off.

12:08.800 --> 12:14.480
On the right, you can see an example of the PWM.

12:16.000 --> 12:24.720
In the six-step for square wave control strategy, the switch is alternately closed and open for a time equal to

12:25.280 --> 12:31.440
T over 2, where T is the period of the alternating output voltage.

12:31.440 --> 12:43.360
The inverter changes state every T over 6 and can assume six different states, called active states.

12:44.080 --> 12:51.040
The amplitude of the output voltage depends only on V and the state of the switches.

12:51.040 --> 12:59.600
If you sum the voltage due to the branch, we can have the voltage fed to the inverter.

13:00.640 --> 13:05.680
Active vehicle propulsion requires the motor drives offering forward motoring,

13:05.680 --> 13:10.320
forward regeneration, backward motoring and backward regeneration.

13:10.320 --> 13:18.240
The forward regeneration is essential to capture the braking energy to increase the driving range per charge

13:18.240 --> 13:21.840
by over 10 percent.

